# Every new file is ignored, so nothing gets committed by accident: an app
# folder moved into a package can carry tokens, history or account details.
# Files git already tracks aren't affected. Add a new one on purpose, one
# file at a time (-f skips this rule, so never point it at a folder):
#
#   dots add -f common/.config/foo/foo.conf
*
# Folders aren't ignored, only files: otherwise git refuses even `git add`
# on a tracked file inside one
!*/
